Influencing Voting Dynamics";}i:2;i:385;}i:10;a:3:{i:0;s:7:"p_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:512;}i:11;a:3:{i:0;s:12:"preformatted";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:571:" Tactic: CoC members may engage in lobbying or backdoor negotiations to sway votes in favor of a particular resolution plan or stakeholder, especially if they have vested interests or relationships with certain resolution applicants.
 Beneficiary: This typically benefits specific resolution applicants or creditors who are in a position to offer favorable terms to influential CoC members.
